# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AI chatbot configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in AI_API_KEY. `.env` is already gitignored,
# so your key will never be committed. Restart `npm run dev` after editing.
#
# The chatbot talks to any provider that supports the OpenAI-compatible
# "chat completions" API — which is nearly all of them. Pick ONE of the free
# options below, uncomment its three lines, and you're done. No code changes.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Option 1: Google Gemini (recommended — free tier, no credit card) ────────
# Get a key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# Free-tier limits and current model names: https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing
#
# Use the `-latest` alias, not a pinned version like `gemini-2.5-flash`. Google
# retires specific versions and blocks them for new keys ("no longer available
# to new users"), which breaks the chat; the alias always points at a live model.
AI_API_KEY=
AI_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai
AI_MODEL=gemini-flash-lite-latest


# ── Option 2: Groq (free tier, extremely fast, no credit card) ───────────────
# Get a key: https://console.groq.com/keys
# Pick a current model from: https://console.groq.com/docs/models
# AI_API_KEY=
# AI_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# AI_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile


# ── Option 3: OpenRouter (aggregates many providers; has free models) ────────
# Get a key: https://openrouter.ai/keys
# Browse free models (their id ends in `:free`): https://openrouter.ai/models
# AI_API_KEY=
# AI_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# AI_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BACKUP PROVIDER (optional, but recommended)
#
# Free tiers are small. Gemini's free daily cap is only 20 requests per day,
# per model — one curious visitor can exhaust it. Fill this in and the server
# automatically retries on the backup whenever the main provider is out of
# quota, so BIA keeps answering instead of clocking out.
#
# It's a completely separate account, so it's a separate quota — no
# quota-dodging, no extra project. Use a DIFFERENT provider than your main one.
#
# Groq is the natural pick: free, no credit card, and very fast.
#   1. Sign up and create a key: https://console.groq.com/keys
#   2. Paste it below and uncomment all three lines
#   3. Confirm the model id is still current: https://console.groq.com/docs/models
#   4. Restart the dev server
#
# Leave AI_FALLBACK_API_KEY empty to disable the fallback entirely.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# AI_FALLBACK_API_KEY=gsk_...paste-your-groq-key-in-.env-NOT-here
# AI_FALLBACK_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# AI_FALLBACK_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile


# Note: free tiers, limits, and model names change over time. If the chat stops
# working, check the provider's model list above and update AI_MODEL.
#
# Quotas are per project PER MODEL, so switching AI_MODEL also gives you a fresh
# daily allowance — handy while developing.
